    I build revenue systems — the pipelines that find leads, score them against an ICP, 
    and put them in front of a rep with enough context to be useful.
    <br />
    <br />
    I got here from both directions. I spent years in US direct sales and property management, learning to build rapport fast and influence outcomes under pressure. 
    Then I moved into data: ETL pipelines, predictive models, marketing analytics. 
    Most people in this work have one half or the other. Having both means I build tooling reps will actually use, because I've been the person whose quota depended on it.
    I work in documented sprints with ADRs and public build logs, and I care more about what ships than about process.
    <br />
    <br />
    Outside of work, I bring the same intentionality to my life that I apply to data. 
    I stay grounded through daily calisthenics, clear my head by traveling, and channel my creativity into cooking, leatherworking, and mixing house music. 
    My most important ongoing project is building a house for my retired parents in Queretaro, and I also spend my time fostering dogs and helping them find new homes.
